The upstream `LICENSE` is retained verbatim in this directory. The four
fields above are machine-read by the `fork-notice` gate in `goal.py check`.

This tree is a liberal in-place fork: upstream files are edited directly. Git
history against the fork base is the complete change record. Every upstream
file a commit after `Import commit` touched carries a prominent Apache-2.0
§4(b) modification notice in-file; §4(b) requires no date.

## Strict compilation path (the Python TCB)

- `src/e_minus_minus/__init__.py` — package initialization (docstring only;
  executes before `strict` under `python3 -m`).
- `src/e_minus_minus/strict.py` — strict compilation entry point.
- `src/e_minus_minus/lexer.py` — lexical analysis.
- `src/e_minus_minus/parser.py` — parsing into the compiler AST.
- `src/e_minus_minus/emitter.py` — Python emission.
- `src/e_minus_minus/ast_nodes.py` — compiler AST definitions.
- `src/e_minus_minus/errors.py` — compiler error definitions.

This list is the complete package: the upstream legacy pipeline
(`transpiler.py`, `normalizer.py`, `resolver.py`, `cli.py`) is deleted in
this fork. `strict.py` still poisons those module names plus `anthropic` in
`sys.modules` as an import backstop.

Strict-profile extensions over upstream: `Use`, `Require that`, and
`Exit with` are statement keywords at head position; top-level imports, dotted
references and call targets are admitted. The language contract is
`docs/spec.md` plus the strict entry point's validation.
